{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>In the midst of all Israel.</b> Wherever one of them was fleeing through the land, it would split open beneath him and swallow him — these are the words of Rabbi Yehudah. Rabbi Nechemiah said to him: But was it not already stated, ״וַתִּפְתַּח הָאָרֶץ אֶת פִּיהָ״ (Numbers 16) — and not 'its mouths'? He said to him: Then how do I fulfill <b>in the midst of all Israel</b>? He said to him: That the earth became a slope like a funnel, and wherever one of them was, he would roll and slide down to the place of the splitting." "<b>And all that stood upon their feet.</b> This is a person's property, which stands him on his feet (Sanhedrin 110)."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:46:30.910042489Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}